WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I got this drone because
I thought when Preeta

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I come into the weddin
on the elephants

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the drone
could be kind of, uh --

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.640 size:84% position:42%
As I'm saying the words
"drone" and "elephant"

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.810
out loud to another human being,
I'm wondering,

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.681 line:92%
is this, um -- is this a lot

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wedding's been --

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're already
stressful enough, you know

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Important part is that Preeta

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.321 line:92%
she can't wait to marry you.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
So just take it easy, you know
Enjoy the ride.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.793 line:92%
You only got one shot at it.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, one chance
to, like, get it right.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:30.463 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
So just go ahead
and pull it back.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:36.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, pull it back
and just sort of let it rip.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Colin Jost

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:42.675
They didn't -- they didn't hav
a clip with Tom or Jerry in it

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.544 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:50.116
-I was told that they would be
making me Tom after the fact

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.753 line:92%
-Oh. Wait! You thought --

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:57.057
You thought this was, like
a motion-capture situation

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I thought that motion -
You know how you normally

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:03.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
put on, like, a powder-blu
motion-capture sweater?

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.633
-Of course.
-That's what I thought that was.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I kept --
And I was like, they'll --

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, I'm just sort o
saying a couple words,

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they'll put in, like,
arms going crazy.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.944 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I do a flip at the end.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
something that makes it fun.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, puts a little
more Tom on it.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:23.550 line:92%
-A little more Tom on it.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.652 size:78% position:39%
That was my number --
When I told friends

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.953 line:92%
I was doing "Tom &amp; Jerry,"

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were like,
"Oh, so are you Tom or Jerry?"

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Oh, I'm, um, neither.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.795 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm just sort of a man."

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.098 line:92%
I'm just, like, a human man.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like, "Oh,
so who's Tom and who's Jerry?"

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "No one.
They just -- They don't talk."

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.673
I'm just -- They're like,
"What are you doing in it?

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, just --
I'm getting married."

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.311
And they're like, "So, like,
what you're doing in real life?"

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.112 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was like, "Yeah.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:55.949
They don't let me really
stretch a lot as an actor.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.749 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's exciting.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:00.186
-You were really entertaining me
talking about --

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:03.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, you and I,
we are desk people.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:03.990 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our best work
has been done sitting.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were saying
that, like, being in a fil

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
with actual actors,
trained actors,

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
actors who have been
in other movies, it really -

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:18.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
the difference
in your skill set was obvious.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I had a lot of scene
with Michael Peña,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:26.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is not only very funny
but a great actor.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we would be in a scene
and there would be,

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
like 200 extras around us.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had obviously been
setting up this whole shot

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the scene and the set
for days, and everyone waiting

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I would come in,
and I would walk into the set,

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:47.066
completely miss my mark,
not even consider where --

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
It never even dawned on me
that there was a mark.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
Walked way past it
up to Michael Peña,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:57.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
start talking to him,
have a long, emotional speech.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:00.813
And he's looking at me like,
"Mm-hmm," just, like, smiling.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.383
And I'm like, "It's weird
that this emotional speech

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
is kind of making him laugh,
but...

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then after the fact,
he's like,

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You were out of focus
the whole --

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.257 size:78% position:39%
You were out of focus
the entire speech."

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:14.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "You just blew
way past your mark.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:18.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
None of the cameras
captured you talking."

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just enjoyed
letting me do it

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he could just
rub it in my face

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how much worse
an actor I am

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:28.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
on just a very basic
"not being on camera" level.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
We normally sit at a desk.
-Yeah.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:33.146
-We don't have to really worry
if we're off a couple inches

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.047 line:92%
It doesn't really matter.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:37.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when there's cameras
that are, apparently, like -

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:40.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
work based on focus and ligh
and things like that,

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when you're not
in those things, it's bad.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:49.529
-Um, hey, this is very rare,
but we just got some news.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.630 line:92%
Andy Samberg has reached out

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.700
He wants you to check your phone
right now.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
All right, well, let me --

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.938 line:92%
I'm filming on it, so hold on.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:03:59.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:04.110
I got to, like, you know,
take "do not disturb" off.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.979 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is going to
really backfire.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Um...

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:16.122 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:19.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just got some texts.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:23.796
"Hey, are you on with Seth
right now for your interview

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:27.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
Reminder to turn off alert
on your laptop."

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.669 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Photo of me.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.672 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"This you?

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.040 line:92%
If you don't turn off alerts

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
it will keep popping up
and interrupting.

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:40.346 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Can be very annoying."

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.215 line:92%
More coming in as I say this

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Anyway, hope you
getting these in real time

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.954 line:92%
so it doesn't become annoyin

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:51.591 size:78% position:39%
if someone texts you
while it's happening.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Might be bad TV.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:58.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nielsen ratings
could get screwy.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:01.200 line:92%
Also, Frisbee sucks, right?"

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughter ]
-"The dog."

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.737 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He specified the dog.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:09.942
The first punctuation he's use
was after "the dog," period.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:13.413 line:92%
"Please respond. Spinning out.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.747 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Spinning out?!

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:18.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Need to know
you hate Frisbee."

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Full disclosure --
on peyote right now.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Don't be mad.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[Bleep] pic?

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.029 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:34.701
-Is he asking if you want on
or is he asking you to send one?

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:37.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.772 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-He says, "Get or send."

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.413 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Huh.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Damn it.
-All right.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He knows --
You know what?

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:55.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
Say what you will about Andy
but he knows the biz.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:56.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He knows the biz.
I mean, the Nielsens part

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:59.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
really talks --
really speaks to how intuitive

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Always obsessed
with the Nielsen numbers.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can we get you back?
Can we get your visual back?

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, there he is.
-Hi, I'm back.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.069 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Andy just texted again,

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Remember to turn
your alerts off.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would hate for it
to mess up Seth's show."

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very kind.
-Yeah, he's thoughtful.

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hi.
-Hi, buddy.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You, um --

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:24.083 size:88% position:44%
I want to ask a question
about your acting range.

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:25.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
As you mentioned,
they didn't ask much of yo

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:26.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "Tom and Jerry"...
-Thanks.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...but you did a politica
impression this year.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to do Pete Buttigieg
-Yes.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now Transportation
Secretary Buttigieg.

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:37.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you guys actually live
in the same dorm

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:40.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
at, uh...
Harvard University?

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:43.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, that's -- that's right
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:46.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you know him
at all in college?

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were in the same dorm
for three years.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:55.047 line:92%
We had a mutual friend who -

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we kind of met
and saw through him.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
We didn't cross paths a lot,
I would say,

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:05.124
because he was more involved
in the college side of things.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:11.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
He perhaps was a more
studious student at college.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:11.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I --

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.634
-Like he wouldn't use like -
he probably learned enough words

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:17.103 line:92%
to not say "studious student."

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.304 size:81% position:41%
-Maybe. I don't know.
I don't want to put --

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:22.208
I don't want to put him on -
make him some kind of elite.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your words.
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.113
No, I'm sure -- let him
run Transportation, yeah.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
I took a subway every day --
okay? -- to high school.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What does he know?

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:34.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-Probably still more.

00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:35.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He -- He was, um...

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:41.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was, uh...
Yeah, he was --

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
I spent a lot of my time,
as you know,

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:45.832 line:92%
in the Lampoon organization,

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:50.303
which i would describe
as kind of Heaven's Gate,

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we got out, like,
right before the mass suicide.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:56.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-All the fun leading up to it.

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:57.577 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:59.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I haven't read much about it,
obviously.

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:00.680 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You can ask Pete.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:03.916
Mayor Pete would probably
know more on this, too.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:05.218 line:92%
But I sense that Heaven's Gate

00:08:05.218 --> 00:08:07.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
was kind of a party,
fun times, right?

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:08.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think
it was a good time.

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:09.689 line:92%
-But of course, the suicide --

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They all went like Nike
shopping together and stuff.

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:15.795
-Yeah, I read the broad strokes.
-Right.

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:18.798 size:84% position:42%
-And the Lampoon was
a little bit like that,

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:23.836
and I think he was more tapped
into human society at Harvard.

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:25.037 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:27.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think he probably
was a --

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.407 line:92%
probably a better student.

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:30.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well,
you both turned out great.

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:33.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
Buddy, it is always
a pleasure to see you.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have a great show this wee
with Nick Jonas.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.116 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That's very exciting.

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:40.253 size:84% position:42%
I love you, and I will
hopefully see you soon.

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Love you, too.
It's great to see you.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:46.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm glad that you have a sho
that we can talk on.

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:47.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Tom and Jerry --"
-Very convenient.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Tom and Jerry: The Movie" --
-And tell --

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:50.530 size:78% position:39% line:92%
